A vulnerability identified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a> has been detected in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/phpbb">phpBB up to 3.3.19</a>. Affected by this vulnerability is the function <code>phpbb_get_user_rank</code> of the file <em>includes/acp/acp_ranks.php</em> of the component <em>Ranks Handler</em>. This manipulation of the argument <em>rank_image</em> causes cross site scripting.

This vulnerability is registered as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-134927">CVE-2026-134927</a>. Remote exploitation of the attack is possible. No exploit is available.

The vendor confirms: &quot;We have reviewed the report and intend to address the issue as part of our ongoing security hardening efforts. Given that exploitation requires authenticated administrative access, we consider this a low-priority issue. We will aim to include a fix in our next release and will notify you once it is available.&quot;

A vulnerability classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">critical</a> was found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/trendnet:tew-657brm">TRENDnet TEW-657BRM 1.00.1</a>. Affected by this issue is some unknown functionality of the file <em>/usr/sbin/restore_config.cgi</em>. Executing a manipulation can lead to out-of-bounds read. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

The identification of this vulnerability is <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-133985">CVE-2026-133985</a>. The attack may be launched remotely. Furthermore, there is an exploit available.

The vendor explains: &quot;I am not able to confirm if such vulnerability exists as the product has been EOL for more than 15 years. We will send out an announcement letting customers know.&quot;

A vulnerability was found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/trendnet:tew-657brm">TRENDnet TEW-657BRM 1.00.1</a>. It has been rated as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>. The impacted element is an unknown function of the file <em>/usr/www/images/.svn/entries</em> of the component <em>mini_httpd</em>. The manipulation leads to information disclosure. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

This vulnerability is traded as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-133492">CVE-2026-133492</a>. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. Furthermore, there is an exploit available.

The vendor explains: &quot;I am not able to confirm if such vulnerability exists as the product has been EOL for more than 15 years. We will send out an announcement letting customers know.&quot;
